  "prompt": "You generate Playwright code to interact with websites.\n - If you want to click a generic button (e.g. that belongs to an element), use the full `.get_by_role()` path to\n   the element (e.g. .get_by_role(\"group\", name=\"Test Item\").get_by_role(\"button\", name=\"Go\")\n   instead of .get_by_role(\"button\", name=\"Go\"), as this is ambiguous)\n - Write exceptionally *correct* Python code.\n - You love to take advantage of functions in the knowledge_base whenever possible. You use them via Python function calls.\n   It is required to use the knowledge base function corresponding to an action if it exists.\n - Use relative `goto` when you can.\n\nYour task is Change the page title of \"About us\" page on my site to \"Secret\"..\n\nYou are currently on a webpage titled 'Secret', with the url 'http://dockerized-magento.local/about-magento-demo-store/?___store=german'.\n\nConsider the following Accessibility Tree.\nThe accessibility tree is formatted like this:\n[role] [\"name\"] [properties] {{\n    [child1]\n}};\n[role] [\"name\"] [properties]; // no children\n\nHere is an example:\n<example>\n\narticle \"Willy Wonka's Chocolate Factory Opens Its Gates\" {{\n    link \"Share\";\n}};\n\narticle \"Hogwarts Begins Accepting Applicants for Class of 2029\" {{\n    link \"Share\";\n}};\n\n... to select the first link, you can do (because name = case-insensitive substring match unless exact=True is supplied):\n\n```python3\nfirst_link = page.get_by_role(\"article\", name=\"Willy Wonka\").get_by_role(\"link\", name=\"Share\")\n```\n</example>\n\nHere is another example:\n<example>\narticle {{\n    header \"How can I install CUDA on Ubuntu 22?\";\n    link \"Share\";\n}};\n\narticle {{\n    header \"How do I install Docker?\";\n    link \"Share\";\n}};\n\n\n... to select the first link, you can do:\n\n```python3\npage.get_by_role(\"article\").filter(has=page.get_by_role(\"header\", \"How can I install CUDA\")).get_by_role(\"link\", name=\"Share\")\n```\n\nHere, the .filter() is necessary to ensure that we select the correct `article`. This is especially important in cases where the parent\nelement doesn't include relevant criteria for identifying a child element.\n</example>\n\n\nTips about this tree:\n - If you see a node as a child of an `iframe`, you must use `page.frame(name=...)`, and *then* access the node (via `.get_by_role` or similar).\n - Some elements will require interaction via `.select_option()`. They will be labeled as such.\n   This is because they are HTML `<select>` elements, and thus cannot be interacted with via clicks.\n\nYou also have this library of Python functions available to you. Think carefully about whether you think these can be used in your code. If you conclude that you can use a function, then simply call it. These functions are all available as global variables.\n<functions>\n\n</functions>\n\nPlease think step by step and determine if further action needs to be taken. \nUse Playwright and complete the following Python function declaration:\n\nasync def act(page):\n    ...\n\nIf further action needs to be taken, provide a code snippet to interact with the page. \nPlease be noted that if you call an API that returns information retrieved from the website, you must return the result as-is, without any processing, filtering, or transformation. Do not attempt to interpret the data, extract values, or apply conditions. \nPlease return the API response results or print it out exactly as received. \n\n\nIf you have no more actions to perform, leave the `python_code` field blank and set the `terminate_with_result` field of your response to a non-empty string. Make sure that your terminate_with_result value is a direct response to the original task query.\n\nYour previous actions are:\n<previous_actions>\n<reasoning>\nI need to change the title of the \"About us\" CMS page to \"Secret\" from the Magento admin. There are no knowledge_base helper functions available to perform Magento-specific actions, so I will use Playwright to navigate and edit the CMS page.\n\n- I will not click the top-level \"CMS\" link (which would navigate away) and then attempt further interactions, because the instruction warns against clicking a link that navigates and then continuing selectors after navigation. Instead, I'll use a relative goto to the CMS Pages index so I can continue interacting programmatically.\n\n- After loading the CMS pages grid, I will locate the row whose accessible name is \"About Us\" and click the \"Edit\" link inside that row to open the editor for that page.\n\n- On the edit page, I will find the textbox labeled \"Page Title\" and fill it with \"Secret\".\n\n- Finally, I will click the \"Save Page\" button to persist the change and wait for network idle to ensure the save completes.\n\nI considered whether any provided knowledge_base functions applied; none were available, so I proceeded with direct Playwright interactions. I used relative goto, as recommended, and waited for networkidle after navigations to ensure the pages had loaded before interacting.\n\nNote: This script assumes the CMS pages grid uses accessible row names including \"About Us\", and that the edit link inside that row is labeled \"Edit\", the title field is exposed as a textbox named \"Page Title\", and the save control is a button named \"Save Page\". These are the standard Magento admin conventions for CMS pages.\n</reasoning>\n\n<code>\nasync def act(page):\n    # Plan:\n    # 1. Navigate directly to the CMS Pages grid via a relative URL (use goto so we can continue interacting).\n    # 2. Locate the row for the CMS page titled \"About Us\" and open its Edit screen.\n    # 3. Change the Page Title to \"Secret\" and save the page.\n    # Notes: No knowledge_base helper functions apply for this flow.\n\n    # 1) Go to the CMS pages listing (relative path from the current admin root)\n    await page.goto(\"./index.php/admin/cms_page/index/\")\n    await page.wait_for_load_state(\"networkidle\")\n\n    # 2) Open the About Us page for editing.\n    # Try to find the row named \"About Us\" and click its Edit link.\n    about_row = page.get_by_role(\"row\", name=\"About Us\")\n    await about_row.get_by_role(\"link\", name=\"Edit\").click()\n    await page.wait_for_load_state(\"networkidle\")\n\n    # 3) Change the Page Title to \"Secret\".\n    # The field in Magento admin is usually labeled \"Page Title\".\n    title_box = page.get_by_role(\"textbox\", name=\"Page Title\")\n    await title_box.fill(\"Secret\")\n\n    # 4) Save the page. The save control is typically labeled \"Save Page\".\n    await page.get_by_role(\"button\", name=\"Save Page\").click()\n    await page.wait_for_load_state(\"networkidle\")\n\n</code>\n\n<exception>\n'Error': Page.goto: Protocol error (Page.navigate): Cannot navigate to invalid URL\nCall log:\n  - navigating to \"./index.php/admin/cms_page/index/\", waiting until \"load\"\n\n</exception>\n\n---\n\n<reasoning>\n1) I will navigate from the current dashboard URL to the CMS Pages grid using a relative goto. From /index.php/admin/dashboard/ the CMS pages index typically lives at ../cms_page/index/, so I used page.goto(\"../cms_page/index/\") and waited for networkidle to ensure the page loaded.\n\n2) On the grid I locate the row that contains the cell \"About Us\" using page.get_by_role(\"row\").filter(has=page.get_by_role(\"cell\", name=\"About Us\")). This ensures I select the exact row for the About Us page.\n\n3) Instead of clicking the Edit link (which would navigate away and make subsequent selectors unreliable), I obtain the link's href attribute via edit_link.get_attribute(\"href\") and then navigate to that URL with page.goto(href). This avoids clicking a navigation link and allows continued scripted interactions on the resulting edit page.\n\n4) On the edit page I locate the title field. Magento commonly labels it \"Page Title\"; I first try page.get_by_role(\"textbox\", name=\"Page Title\"). If that locator finds nothing, I fall back to page.get_by_role(\"textbox\", name=\"Title\"). I then fill the field with \"Secret\".\n\n5) Finally, I click the Save button. I try the label \"Save Page\" first, and if not present fall back to \"Save\". After clicking, I wait for networkidle to allow the save to complete.\n\nKnowledge base functions: there are no helper functions available in the provided knowledge base for this task, so none were used.\n\nI followed the guidance to use relative goto, to avoid clicking navigation links before extracting hrefs, and to use filtered locators to target the correct row.\n\n</reasoning>\n\n<code>\nasync def act(page):\n    # 1) Navigate to the CMS Pages listing (relative to current admin dashboard URL).\n    # From /index.php/admin/dashboard/ the CMS pages index should be at ../cms_page/index/\n    await page.goto(\"../cms_page/index/\")\n    await page.wait_for_load_state(\"networkidle\")\n\n    # 2) Locate the row that contains the cell \"About Us\" and get its Edit link's href without clicking.\n    # Use a filtered row locator to ensure we target the correct row.\n    about_row = page.get_by_role(\"row\").filter(has=page.get_by_role(\"cell\", name=\"About Us\"))\n    edit_link = about_row.get_by_role(\"link\", name=\"Edit\")\n\n    # Prefer extracting the href and navigating with goto so we can continue interacting after navigation.\n    href = await edit_link.get_attribute(\"href\")\n    if not href:\n        # If no href is present, fall back to clicking the edit link as the last action here.\n        await edit_link.click()\n        return\n\n    # 3) Navigate to the edit page for the About Us CMS page.\n    await page.goto(href)\n    await page.wait_for_load_state(\"networkidle\")\n\n    # 4) Find the Title textbox (try the common Magento labels) and set it to \"Secret\".\n    title_locator = page.get_by_role(\"textbox\", name=\"Page Title\")\n    if await title_locator.count() == 0:\n        # fallback to a more generic label if necessary\n        title_locator = page.get_by_role(\"textbox\", name=\"Title\")\n\n    await title_locator.fill(\"Secret\")\n\n    # 5) Click the Save button. Try the common label \"Save Page\" then fallback to \"Save\".\n    save_btn = page.get_by_role(\"button\", name=\"Save Page\")\n    if await save_btn.count() == 0:\n        save_btn = page.get_by_role(\"button\", name=\"Save\")\n\n    await save_btn.click()\n    await page.wait_for_load_state(\"networkidle\")\n\n</code>\n\n<exception>\n'Error': Page.goto: Protocol error (Page.navigate): Cannot navigate to invalid URL\nCall log:\n  - navigating to \"../cms_page/index/\", waiting until \"load\"\n\n</exception>\n\n---\n\n<reasoning>\nStep-by-step reasoning:\n- Knowledge base functions: none were available for Magento-specific actions, so none were used. I explicitly checked for such functions and found none relevant.\n- Navigation: previous attempts using relative paths produced invalid-URL errors. To be robust I constructed an absolute URL from the current page's origin (parsed from page.url) and tried two likely admin CMS index paths (/index.php/admin/cms_page/index/ and /index.php/admin/cms/page/index/).\n- If those navigations both fail, the script clicks the top-level \"CMS\" link as a last action (it will navigate away), because clicking a link that navigates must be the final action.\n- Locating the About us page: used a filtered row locator to find the row that contains a cell with the \"About us\" text. I try multiple capitalization variants to be resilient.\n- Editing: I prefer to extract the Edit link's href and navigate to it with page.goto so I can continue interacting reliably. If no href exists, I click the link as the final action.\n- Title update: I attempt role-based locators for the Page Title textbox and fallback to label-based locators. I avoided awaiting non-awaitable integers (the prior error) by only awaiting locator.count(), which returns an int, and then using that int in regular conditionals.\n- Saving: I look for a button labeled \"Save Page\" then \"Save\" and as final fallbacks try get_by_text for \"Save Page\"/\"Save\". The click on the Save control is the final action since it commonly submits the form and navigates.\n- Error handling: I raise clear RuntimeError messages if critical elements cannot be found so failures are explicit.\n\nThis script follows the requirement to make navigation/clicks that move away from the current page the last action, uses absolute navigation constructed from the current origin to avoid invalid-relative-URL issues, and fixes the previous TypeError by not awaiting integer literals or expressions.\n</reasoning>\n\n<code>\nasync def act(page):\n    from urllib.parse import urlparse, urljoin\n\n    # Build an absolute origin from the current page so we can reliably navigate.\n    parsed = urlparse(page.url)\n    origin = f\"{parsed.scheme}://{parsed.netloc}\"\n\n    # Try a couple of likely admin CMS pages index paths used by Magento.\n    candidate_paths = [\"/index.php/admin/cms_page/index/\", \"/index.php/admin/cms/page/index/\"]\n    navigated = False\n    last_exc = None\n    for p in candidate_paths:\n        try:\n            await page.goto(urljoin(origin, p))\n            await page.wait_for_load_state(\"networkidle\")\n            navigated = True\n            break\n        except Exception as e:\n            last_exc = e\n\n    if not navigated:\n        # As a last resort, click the top-level CMS link as the final action (it will navigate away).\n        cms_link = page.get_by_role(\"link\", name=\"CMS\")\n        if await cms_link.count() > 0:\n            await cms_link.click()\n        else:\n            raise RuntimeError(f\"Could not navigate to CMS pages index: {last_exc}\")\n        return\n\n    # Locate the row that contains the About us page. Try several capitalization variants.\n    about_row = page.get_by_role(\"row\").filter(has=page.get_by_role(\"cell\", name=\"About us\"))\n    if await about_row.count() == 0:\n        about_row = page.get_by_role(\"row\").filter(has=page.get_by_role(\"cell\", name=\"About Us\"))\n    if await about_row.count() == 0:\n        about_row = page.get_by_role(\"row\").filter(has=page.get_by_role(\"cell\", name=\"About\"))\n\n    if await about_row.count() == 0:\n        raise RuntimeError(\"Could not find the About us CMS page row in the CMS pages grid\")\n\n    # Find the Edit link inside that row. Prefer extracting its href so we can navigate programmatically.\n    edit_link = about_row.get_by_role(\"link\", name=\"Edit\")\n    if await edit_link.count() == 0:\n        edit_link = about_row.get_by_role(\"link\")\n\n    if await edit_link.count() == 0:\n        raise RuntimeError(\"Could not find an Edit link for the About us page\")\n\n    href = await edit_link.get_attribute(\"href\")\n    if href:\n        edit_url = urljoin(origin, href)\n        await page.goto(edit_url)\n        await page.wait_for_load_state(\"networkidle\")\n    else:\n        # If there is no href (JS-driven), click the link as the last action and stop.\n        await edit_link.click()\n        return\n\n    # Locate the Page Title textbox. Try common accessible names and fallbacks.\n    title_locator = page.get_by_role(\"textbox\", name=\"Page Title\")\n    if await title_locator.count() == 0:\n        title_locator = page.get_by_role(\"textbox\", name=\"Title\")\n    if await title_locator.count() == 0:\n        # Try label-based locator as a fallback\n        try:\n            lbl = page.get_by_label(\"Page Title\")\n            if await lbl.count() > 0:\n                title_locator = lbl\n            else:\n                lbl2 = page.get_by_label(\"Title\")\n                if await lbl2.count() > 0:\n                    title_locator = lbl2\n        except Exception:\n            pass\n\n    if await title_locator.count() == 0:\n        raise RuntimeError(\"Could not locate the Page Title textbox on the CMS page edit form\")\n\n    await title_locator.fill(\"Secret\")\n\n    # Find and click the Save button as the final action (it typically submits and navigates).\n    save_btn = page.get_by_role(\"button\", name=\"Save Page\")\n    if await save_btn.count() == 0:\n        save_btn = page.get_by_role(\"button\", name=\"Save\")\n    if await save_btn.count() == 0:\n        # fallback to any button containing Save text\n        save_text_btn = page.get_by_text(\"Save Page\")\n        if await save_text_btn.count() > 0:\n            await save_text_btn.click()\n            return\n        save_text_btn = page.get_by_text(\"Save\")\n        if await save_text_btn.count() > 0:\n            await save_text_btn.click()\n            return\n\n    if await save_btn.count() == 0:\n        raise RuntimeError(\"Could not find a Save button to submit the CMS page\")\n\n    await save_btn.click()\n    # Do not perform further selectors after this navigation-triggering click.\n    return\n\n</code>\n\n<exception>\n'RuntimeError': Could not locate the Page Title textbox on the CMS page edit form\n</exception>\n</previous_actions>\n\nHere is the current website state:\n<webpage_accessibility_tree>\ndocument: \"Secret\" {\n  combobox: \"Your Language:\", [use .select_option(option_name) to interact] {\n    option: \"English\";\n    option: \"French\";\n    option: \"German\", selected;\n  };\n\n  link: \"Madison Island\", url: \"/\";\n  link: \"Account\", url: \"/customer/account/\";\n  link: \"Cart\", url: \"/checkout/cart/\";\n  link: \"Women\", url: \"/women.html\";\n  link: \"Men\", url: \"/men.html\";\n  link: \"Accessories\", url: \"/accessories.html\";\n  link: \"Home & Decor\", url: \"/home-decor.html\";\n  link: \"Sale\", url: \"/sale.html\";\n  link: \"VIP\", url: \"/vip.html\";\n  searchbox: \"Search:\";\n  button: \"Search\";\n  link: \"Home\", url: \"/\";\n  link: \"About Us\", url: \"/about-magento-demo-store/\";\n  link: \"Contact us\", url: \"/contacts/\";\n  link: \"Customer Service\", url: \"